WEBVTT

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:24.090
"University of Rome"

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.170
Are you really dropping
out of school, Caterina?

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:32.500
Yeah. I turned in the documents just now.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.510
This is so sudden...

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.670
You could've come to me about it...

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.200
I'm sorry, Patrizia.
But I've made up my mind.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.690
You can't just take some time off?

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.420
I can't be wishy-washy about this.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.860
I am taking the country to court.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.300
If it goes to trial, can you win?

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.530
My father's lawyer and
acquaintances are going to help me.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.530
I won't lose.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:15.710
Say, how did things turn out
with that officer at the Pantheon?

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.880
Oh, he asks me out often.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.890
Oh, better than I thought, then!

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:26.050
He was so persistent, so he
seemed iffy to me at first!

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:35.070
I have you to thank. You went to
the movies with us the first time...

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.070
Is he a nicer person than you thought?

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:39.240
Yeah.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.900
I went through all that trouble,
so you two better get along!

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:51.520
Amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:01:51.520 --> 00:02:06.560
I want to protect you and fulfill
my promise to the only one for me

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:14.040
In a world filled with doubt,
I still can't find the answer

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:21.110
Even so, I continue forward... Why?

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:31.560
If I can change this dream-like
reality with my own two hands,

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:39.060
amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:46.740
I want to protect the only one for me

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:54.580
I swear on my beating heart I will
continue to run until I burn away

00:02:54.580 --> 00:03:02.090
Amid the eternal love
I feel simply by living,

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:11.390
I want to fulfill my promise

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:52.300
He's always like that, isn't he?

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.200
He's an odd one.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.710
We've been here a month,

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:05.850
but he still won't come out of his shell.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:13.220
He probably doesn't value much
in life or feel happiness often.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.560
It's funny hearing that from you.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.120
Well, I should get going.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:43.220
You get the documents ready, okay?

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.760
Are you going to see Nino in Rome?

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.250
Yeah. I wonder how he's doing.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:56.250
"Caterina and the Circle of Revenge"

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.040
I don't like this.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.010
Yeah, I bet.

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:05.210
But you'll understand someday.

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.140
How can you be so sure?

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.610
Franca. What is it you're fighting against?

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.780
When will victory be yours?

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.920
To avenge your old man...

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:20.790
...who will you have to kill first?

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.110
Think that over now, while you can.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:41.640
Before you turn into an old dog
like me that can't run anymore.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:47.140
Nino, you were weak, that's all.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:58.260
Caterina, I'm sorry about your father.

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:01.770
To think he would die in prison...

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:08.040
Uncle Marinov. Were my
father's charges fabricated?

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:12.940
He wasn't someone like me,
who's connected to the underworld.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:16.850
There are too many suspicious
things about the charges against him.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:26.350
What do you intend to do now?

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.870
I won't give up.

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:48.010
It's good to see you again, Uncle Marinov.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:51.180
You've really grown, Caterina.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:53.180
I didn't think you had it in you

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:58.880
when you declared you were going
to become an activist 8 years ago.

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:04.230
So, did you find out anything
about your father afterward?

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:08.270
No, that's not what I focus on now...

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:11.720
Revenge, rather than exposing the truth?

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:18.140
Are you working with
Cristiano of Milan now?

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:20.610
- Yes.
- Be careful.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.850
The northern isolationists are
fighting the government in the open,

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:27.350
and are also in the middle
of an internal power struggle.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:30.340
Don't get caught up in any petty fighting.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.970
Hey, Jeremiah.

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:49.310
That woman is Franca!

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:50.770
Say what?

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:53.080
It's definitely her.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:56.810
The one Special Ops Section 2 had
a scuffle with in Montalcino recently.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.680
The woman on the wanted posters?

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.850
Why did she come to see that broker?

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:04.720
It doesn't matter.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:07.930
Hello? Irma? Where are you?

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:11.830
Driving around the highway loop.
Near the airport.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:15.670
We found a wanted Padania
agent at our stakeout location.

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:19.270
I assume Vito's with you? Let's meet up.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.410
Got it.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:22.510
What're we gonna do?

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:27.640
What do you think we're
gonna do? Catch her, obviously.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:31.280
Leave.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:36.150
I'm not teaching anyone. I've given it up.

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:41.830
Franco-san! I heard your grandfather
was a legendary bomb crafter!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.160
He trained you to make
bombs too, didn't he?!

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:53.000
I never really wanted to make bombs.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:56.310
I just helped him, that's all.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:09:02.010
And he died last month.
There's no reason to continue.

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:06.850
Leave. Before it gets dark.

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:24.520
Did you even hear what I said?

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:32.680
Those with power are
obligated to use their skills!

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:37.180
Power? I have no power.

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.050
All anyone needs now

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:43.420
are simple bombs that can
be detonated by cell phone.

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:48.160
My grandfather devoted himself
to handcrafted bomb-making,

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:51.560
but that's all out of date now.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:55.900
Who told you about me?

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:59.770
Angelo Marinov, of Rome...

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:01.370
Marinov, huh?

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.370
Then you must've been sent here

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:07.910
after being turned down by plenty of others.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:15.580
Otherwise, you never would've
come to someone as useless as me.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:26.030
What's your goal? What is an
amateur girl like you plotting?

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:29.100
My father was thrown in prison
for crimes he didn't commit!

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:32.590
I took the case to court,
but he died while in prison!

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.770
You're going to get revenge?

00:10:35.770 --> 00:10:38.610
I'm going to change this unjust world!

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:46.440
Then become a religious
person or something.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.490
Don't touch me, you drunk!

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:56.460
Acting like you know everything
even though you do nothing!

00:10:56.460 --> 00:11:00.620
There's nothing for me
to learn from you anyway!

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:16.470
Hey!

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.820
Help! My wife needs help!

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.120
What's wrong?!

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:27.650
Our car broke down on
the way to the hospital!

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:39.670
This looks bad!

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.660
We'll take her in my car!

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.180
Don't move!

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.010
What's going on?

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:51.010
I'm going to get Franca.

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:52.510
Did something happen?

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:57.050
The car is off the highway
and hasn't moved at all.

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:58.350
Is she in danger?

00:12:58.350 --> 00:13:00.410
Probably.

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:16.330
It's her, alright. Franca of the Padania.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:20.570
This is big. Let's inform the chief right away.

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:23.240
Don't be in such a rush, Irma.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:27.540
If we haul her back to headquarters,
Public Safety's gonna take her.

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:30.410
Why not have her talk while we can?

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:35.320
Do whatever. But I'm still
going to make a report.

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:36.590
Matthias!

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:38.050
Y-Yeah?

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:41.790
- Take her stuff upstairs.
- Got it.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:54.500
Say, Irma. Are you sure about this?

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:55.740
About what?

00:13:55.740 --> 00:14:00.740
You don't think Jeremiah
might kill her, do you?

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:03.380
Have trust in your associates.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:06.020
It was for your sake that he...

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:07.680
No, never mind.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:10.450
Let's let him unwind a bit to feel better.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:24.570
I have nothing to tell you!

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:27.830
Good, because I have nothing to ask you.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:34.910
I just want to make you hurt.

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:39.850
You're a real goodie-two-shoes
to fall for that lame act.

00:14:41.050 --> 00:14:43.850
So the pregnant girl was fake, too?

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:48.060
Thank good...

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:50.190
Irma, the "pregnant girl,"

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:54.160
nearly died three years ago
because of one of your bombs!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:58.190
There's still shrapnel in her stomach!

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:00.440
While I'm at it,

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:05.510
I should mention I lost my left eye
and two fingers at the same place!

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.530
So, what do you think about that?!

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:13.820
I asked you what you think about that!

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:18.760
Everyone carries
around hatred of some sort...

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:24.560
If you think you're special in any
way, you're gravely mistaken...

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:49.970
Matthias?!

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:45.840
His student? You?

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:50.030
Nino, was it? What's so funny?

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:55.380
I just find it hard to believe
Franco can teach a woman anything!

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.080
Right, Brother?

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:00.680
I thought you quit the
bomb-making business?

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:03.950
So what happened? Love at first sight?

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:07.390
How rude! Let's go, Franco!

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:11.720
Calm down, Miss. What's your name?

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.060
It's Franca.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:22.730
What's that? An alias? It's a masterpiece!

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:27.980
Franco...

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:30.740
Franca! You're conscious?!

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:33.850
You alright?

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:36.090
Yeah...

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.750
Damn him...

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:47.430
Feeling any better now?

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:13.450
Hey, isn't that Irma?!

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:15.990
Too late. She's dead.

00:19:15.990 --> 00:19:18.460
Damn the Padania...

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:21.460
Hey!

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:25.800
Not good!

00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:51.490
Henrietta! Can you stand?!

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:59.770
Thanks! You saved our lives!

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:00.930
Yes, sir!

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:06.840
That's a cruel trap,
using the corpse like that...

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:10.180
Sounds like something they would enjoy!

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:11.670
Giuse-san?

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:23.130
Are you all right, Hirscher-san?!

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:24.680
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.690
Triela! You're bleeding!

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:33.190
I'm fine. It's just a scratch.

00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:39.580
Hirscher! You okay?!

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:42.700
Yeah! We're both all right!

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.880
He was here...

00:21:11.340 --> 00:21:13.580
You ran into some real trouble.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:16.240
They'll get what's coming to them.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:24.750
Franco.

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:30.130
Thanks for coming to help me.

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:34.060
Hopefully this serves as
a lesson not to act alone.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:38.370
Yeah. I'll stay quiet for a while.

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:41.270
Until we destroy the bridge, anyway.

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:45.480
Where are you going?

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:47.270
The hallway.

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:50.850
Pinocchio. I owe you thanks, too.

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:53.580
You really came through for me.

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.550
Yeah, I guess.

00:21:55.550 --> 00:21:58.950
It's good you didn't die.

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:35.860
Uncle!

00:22:35.860 --> 00:22:37.130
What are you doing here?!

00:22:37.130 --> 00:22:43.660
I received word from Marinov.
I came to check on Franca.

00:22:49.670 --> 00:22:51.510
Is she in here?

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:53.000
Yes.

00:22:54.980 --> 00:22:59.820
I hear you hesitated to kill in Montalcino.

00:22:59.820 --> 00:23:01.350
That was because...

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:06.190
A hired killer is done for
if he hesitates even once.

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:23.140
Well, no matter.
I hear you saved Franca today.

00:23:23.140 --> 00:23:25.810
Well done.

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:28.370
Yes, Uncle!

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:57.740
A doll without a heart,
born from warm hands

00:23:57.740 --> 00:24:07.050
I neither smile nor talk

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:15.320
I want you to hear about
these feelings someday,

00:24:15.320 --> 00:24:23.370
though they can't be put into words

00:24:23.370 --> 00:24:31.540
I'll summon all my strength

00:24:31.540 --> 00:24:44.480
to know what it means to live

00:24:59.930 --> 00:25:04.970
"A Day in the Life of Claes"
